    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters June 10th looking to capitalize on high-upside matchups, headlined by **Josh Naylor** (78.46) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (71.38). **Josh Naylor** is our premier play, benefiting from a massive +16% park adjustment and a soft matchup against Young, whose 4.69 xERA provides the perfect runway for a big day. Similarly, **Tyler Soderstrom** and **James Wood** (70.46) are high-efficiency starts; **James Wood** remains a priority despite the left-on-left disadvantage against Ray, as his elite .403 xwOBA and lead-off spot in the order provide sufficient volume to outweigh the platoon risk. **Corbin Carroll** (67.03) rounds out our top-tier outfield, with his score bolstered specifically by the opponent's \"slow delivery\" profile, which significantly enhances his chances of swiping a bag\u2014a critical factor given our aggressive pursuit of the scarcity category, Stolen Bases.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the morning involved **Vinnie Pasquantino** (49.14), who barely missed the cut. While his underlying metrics remain stable, the optimizer favored our active starters due to a heavy -15% drag caused by his platoon disadvantage against Gore. We elected to keep **Jose Caballero** (55.09) in the lineup instead, as his +13% platoon edge against a lefty keeps his daily floor higher than the alternative. We are monitoring **Dalton Rushing** (48.02) closely; while he is currently active, his position at the bottom of the order (-6%) and the challenge of facing Jones limits his ceiling today. Should we see any late-afternoon lineup shifts for **Giancarlo Stanton** or **Max Muncy**, we may look to swap out our lower-scoring utility pieces to maximize our game cap efficiency.",
